<!--
    kuna GH-271: "15-byte multi-prefix NOP fails SLEIGH decode: body dropped,
    guard inverted"

    clang emits a 15-byte NOP as loop-alignment padding at -O2: six 0x66
    operand-size prefixes, a 0x2e CS segment override, then `0f 1f /4` with SIB
    and disp32, the x86 encoding-length maximum.  That instruction failed to
    decode.  `ParserContext` buffers MAX_INSTRUCTION_LEN (16) bytes and guards
    only the *start* byte of a read, but C++ `PatternBlock::isInstructionMatch`
    walks a pattern in 4-byte chunks whatever its real width, so matching a
    15-byte instruction issues a 4-byte read at offset 13, one byte past the
    buffer.  Upstream reads adjacent struct memory there (UB) and the caller's
    mask discards it; kuna raised BadData, so `FlowInfo` planted an artificial
    halt at the NOP address and truncated the rest of the function.  With the
    padding sitting ahead of a loop head, everything after it (the loop, the
    stores, and any parameter only the loop reads) vanished from the emitted C,
    leaving a bare early-exit shell.

    Fix (kuna GH-271): instruction bytes past the buffer read as 0, the
    deterministic equivalent of the masked-off garbage C++ reads.  The start-byte
    guard is untouched, so a genuinely over-length encoding still errors (pinned
    by decompiler/crates/kuna-sleigh/tests/x86_maxlen_nop_regression.rs).

    Bytes at 0x1000, a shrink-wrapped void f(...) matching the reported shape:
        1000  48 39 0e              CMP  qword ptr [RSI],RCX   ; guard, before
        1003  0f 83 1f 00 00 00     JNC  0x1028                ; the prologue
        1009  53                    PUSH RBX
        100a  48 8b 06              MOV  RAX,qword ptr [RSI]
        100d  66 66 66 66 66 66 2e 0f 1f 84 00 00 00 00 00     ; THE TRIGGER
        101c  48 8b 00              MOV  RAX,qword ptr [RAX]   ; loop head
        101f  48 85 c0              TEST RAX,RAX
        1022  75 f8                 JNZ  0x101c
        1024  48 89 02              MOV  qword ptr [RDX],RAX   ; the dropped store
        1027  5b                    POP  RBX
        1028  c3                    RET                        ; shared return

    Stage: S1 decode (porting-divergence correctness fix, no option).  This
    testcase asserts the FIXED decode: the padding is one 15-byte instruction,
    the stream realigns onto the loop head at 0x101c, and the emitted C keeps
    both the loop and the store that live past the padding.
-->
